{"duration_api_ms":22991,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"37975a69-946f-4e6b-b895-5261b0432d13","total_cost_usd":0.1211172,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10811,"cache_read_input_tokens":118411,"output_tokens":2167,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":685},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10811},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":2167,"cacheReadInputTokens":118411,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10811,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1211172,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":685,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The recovery middleware now handles a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` the same way it already handles a broken connection: it logs a one-line message without a stack trace, records the error with `c.Error`, and calls `c.Abort()` instead of returning a 500. Go's own `net/http` server doesn't print a stack trace for this value either, since it's the standard way to abort a handler on purpose. `go vet` and the recovery/panic tests pass.\n\n**Not committed:** the commit failed because git has no author name or email set in this environment. I didn't set one for you. The changes are staged, so once you've set `user.name` and `user.email` you can commit with your message:\n```\ngit commit -m \"fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover\"\n```\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`recovery.go`**: the check uses `errors.Is`, so a wrapped `ErrAbortHandler` is caught too.\n- **`recovery_test.go`**: new test `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` checks three things: the status set before the panic is kept, the error is logged, and the full \"panic recovered\" stack log isn't written.\n\n**Design choice:** I swallow the panic rather than re-raising it. Re-raising would match `net/http` more closely, because the server would then cut off the connection. As it is, the client gets whatever was already written plus normal completion. I went with swallowing because it matches the \"suppress\" in your message and how broken pipes are handled. Re-raising is a small change if you'd prefer that.","ttft_ms":1726,"type":"result","duration_ms":30684,"uuid":"1819bb73-5874-4987-908d-3c1dc75e9651","ttft_stream_ms":1005,"time_to_request_ms":108,"first_content_frame_ms":1005,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
